  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN256.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">tōḻi talaimakaṟku vāyiṉ maṟuttatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">How the confidante refused the door to HIM.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN256.1">
        <l>piṇaṅkaril vaḷḷai nīṭilaip potumpiṉ</l>
        <l>maṭituyiṉ muṇaiiya vaḷḷukir yāmai</l>
        <l>noṭiviṭu kalliṟ pōki yakaṉṟuṟaip</l>
        <l>pakuvāy niṟaiya nuṅkiṟ kaḷḷi</l>
        <l>ṉukarvā raruntu makiḻpiyaṅku naṭaiyoṭu</l>
        <l>tīmperum paḻaṉa muḻakki yayala</l>
        <l>tāmpaṉ mellaṭai yoṭuṅku mūra</l>
        <l>poyyā laṟiviṉiṉ māya matuvē</l>
        <l>kaiyakap paṭṭamai yaṟiyāy neru<supplied>ṉai</supplied></l>
        <l>maiyeḻi luṇkaṇ maṭantaiyoṭu vaiyai</l>
        <l>yērtaru putuppuṉa luritaṉi ṉukarntatu</l>
        <l>parattai yāyaṅ karappavu mollātu</l>
        <l>kavvaiyā kiṉṟāṟ peritē kāṇṭakat</l>
        <l>tolpukaḻ <anchor n="1"/>niṟainta palpūṅ kaḻaṉik</l>
        <l>karumpayal paṭappaip perumpeyark kaḷḷūrt</l>
        <l>tirunutaṟ kuṟumaka ḷaṇinalam vavviya</l>
        <l>vaṟaṉi lāḷa ṉaṟiyē ṉeṉṟa</l>
        <l>tiṟaṉil veñcū ḷaṟikari <anchor n="2"/>ka<supplied>ṭāa</supplied>y</l>
        <l>muṟiyār peruṅkiḷai ceṟiyap paṟṟi</l>
        <l>nīṟutalaip peyta ñāṉṟai</l>
        <l>vīṟucā lavaiyattā rārppiṉum peritē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="7d">Oh man from a village,</l>
        <l corresp="2">where the sharp-nailed tortoise that disliked drowsy sleep</l>
        <l corresp="1">in the grove with long leaves of the Vaḷḷai in an interlacing thicket</l>
        <l corresp="3">went onto the creaking stones in the wide ghat,</l>
        <l corresp="4">when [its] split mouth was filled from the toddy of the Palmyra fruit,</l>
        <l corresp="5">with the swaying gait of intoxication, [as] of those who drink,</l>
        <l>ravaged the sweet big tank [and] shrank [into its shell]</l>
        <l corresp="6-7c">in the soft leaves of the white waterlily in the neighbourhood,</l>
        <l corresp="8">lie indeed are your charming [words] to [my] knowledge. That that</l>
        <l corresp="9">has fallen into [my] hands, you don’t know. Yesterday,</l>
        <l corresp="11">[your] rightfully enjoying the rising new flood</l>
        <l corresp="10">of the Vaiyai with a young woman with dark graceful kajal eyes</l>
        <l corresp="12">[her] courtesan companions concealing it, too, was not possible;</l>
        <l corresp="13a-c">it became a great scandal</l>
        <l corresp="21">– greater than the din of those in the excellent assembly</l>
        <l corresp="20cd">on the day when,</l>
        <l corresp="15">in Kaḷḷūr of great name, with gardens beneighboured to sugarcane</l>
        <l corresp="13d-14">[and] paddy fields with many flowers, that was filled with ancient fame, so as to be fit to be seen,</l>
        <l corresp="19">they seized [a man] in order to tie [him] to a big branch full of shoots,</l>
        <l corresp="18">invoking a witness who knew of [his] keen oath devoid of substance,</l>
        <l corresp="17">that claimed “I don’t know [her]”, a virtueless man</l>
        <l corresp="16">who had snatched the beauty that adorned a little girl with luminous forehead,</l>
        <l rend="indent3" corresp="20ab">[and] poured ashes on [his] head.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
